### What Would Make This Wrong

The following are structured falsification conditions — scenarios that would materially change the deal rationale or valuation. Validate each before finalizing deal terms.

**Clinical / scientific risks:**
1. **Phase transition failure:** Asset has P(success) of {{ "%.0f"|format(d.combined_pos_pct | default(0)) }}% through approval. A negative Ph{{ d.stage | replace("phase_", "") | replace("_", "/") }} readout invalidates comps-based valuation entirely — comp set prices expected success, not failure.
2. **Endpoint selection:** If the primary endpoint does not map to the endpoints used by comparable trials (e.g., biomarker vs. clinical outcome), regulators may require additional confirmatory trials, extending timeline by 2–4 years.
3. **Safety surprise:** Comps with clean safety profiles command 1.5–3× valuation premiums over those with boxed warnings or REMS. Any on-target toxicity signal not present in comparable programs would displace the asset to the low end of the P25 band or below.

**Market / commercial risks:**
4. **Competitive entrants:** If {{ d.n_competitors | default("2+") }} additional competitors reach approval before this asset, peak penetration assumptions shrink. Each additional approved entrant in the same class typically compresses market share by 20–40%.
5. **Pricing / payer pressure:** Comparable EVs assume current reimbursement trajectories. A 20–30% reduction in net pricing (IRA negotiation, formulary exclusion) would compress the EV/peak-sales multiple by ~0.3–0.7× vs. comp median.
6. **Peak-sales miss:** The rNPV model assumes peak penetration of {{ "%.0f"|format(market.peak_penetration * 100) }}% of TAM (~${{ "%.0f"|format(d.peak_sales_millions | default(0)) }}M peak sales). A 30% downside on penetration alone reduces EV by ~${{ "%.0f"|format(d.rnpv_millions * 0.3 | default(0)) }}M in model terms.

**Structural / deal risks:**
7. **Alternative deals:** If the target signs an exclusivity arrangement with another acquirer or licenses key IP to a third party before close, the comparable deal framework may not reflect the post-encumbrance value.
8. **IP expiry / freedom-to-operate:** Comp set assumes clean IP position. If a key patent is invalidated or generic entry occurs earlier than modeled (before year {{ market.patent_life_years }}), comp-based EV bands are overstated.
{% if comps.match_tier == "phase_only" %}
9. **Match quality caveat:** Comp set is matched on phase only (not indication or therapeutic area). EV/peak-sales multiples for this therapeutic area ({{ d.therapeutic_area | replace("_", " ") | title }}) may differ materially from the cross-indication phase-only median of {{ "%.2fx"|format(comps.peer_median_ev_to_peak_sales) }}. Request indication-specific BD research before finalizing term sheet.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

