## Appendix D: Methodology

**rNPV:** Probability-weighted DCF. Trial costs discounted at phase midpoint, weighted by P(reaching each phase). Revenue modeled as EBIT (net revenue − COGS − SG&A), discounted at {{ d.discount_rate_pct }} WACC over a {{ market.patent_life_years }}-year commercial horizon.

**POS model:** Industry-prior phase transition rates (Biomedtracker/IQVIA 2021, by therapeutic area) adjusted in log-odds space for: endpoint type, MoA precedent, sample adequacy, safety profile, biomarker selection, and competitive pressure. Each adjuster shifts P by ±10–25pp around the base rate.

**Monte Carlo ({{ "%.0f"|format(d.mc_n_simulations | default(10000)) }} simulations):** Phase success ~ Beta(α, β) from analyst mean + ESS; peak sales ~ log-normal (CV={{ "%.0f"|format(mc.std_millions / mc.mean_millions * 100 if mc.mean_millions else 30) }}%); discount rate ~ Normal(μ, 2pp); years-to-peak ~ Normal(μ, 1.5 yrs). Correlated draws via Gaussian copula (peak_sales ↔ penetration ρ = −0.20).

**Scenario analysis:** Bull/base/bear applied as multiplicative shocks to peak sales (×1.5/1.0/0.55), POS (×1.3/1.0/0.70), duration (−0.5/0/+1.0 yrs), and WACC (−1pp/0/+2pp).

